Most SocialFi projects today follow a predictable, fleeting pattern: they hand out points, engineer viral mechanics, and ride a wave of hype for a few months. But once the rewards dry up, users vanish because there was never any real value inside.

@DlicomApp is consciously taking a different path. Instead of chasing temporary hype, they are focusing on three pillars of sustainability:

​Low Friction: Making it effortless for anyone to get started and stay.

​Genuine Retention: Building a product so convenient that users return for the utility, not just an airdrop.

​Long-Term Vision: A strategy that doesn't depend on seasonal trends but on lasting value.

​While others chase "pretty" MAU statistics, Dlicom is obsessing over User Experience. By integrating seamless chats, calls, tipping, a self-custody wallet, and a built-in browser into one place, they’ve removed the complexity of Web3.

​They aren't trying to be "just another Telegram with points." They are building a platform people will use consistently, even when the rewards stop. In the long run, those are the projects that survive.

​If you’re looking for a real blockchain-based social platform rather than a quick farming opportunity, Dlicom is undoubtedly one of the most thoughtful options out there.

@DlicomApp 

